<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wizinv (230)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>wizinv                     (on at level 219, or off)
wizinv &lt;level&gt;             (0 for off)
wizinv &lt;something&gt; [&lt;level&gt;]
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>wizinv
wizinv 240
wizinv chest 230
</pre>
<p>Makes you wizard-invisible: no one below the level you choose can see 
you, not even with see invisible. wizinv alone makes you invisible to 
everyone below level 220 (your level is set to 219), or makes you 
visible again if you were invisible. With a number, you choose the 
level; 0 makes you visible.
</p><p>You can do the same to something or someone else in the world: name it, 
and give a level, or none to switch it between 219 and visible. You can't 
choose a level above your own.
</p><p>Gods see "(wizinv)" after invisible things in their inventory, and a * 
in <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Users</a>. While you are invisible above level 200, your words 
on the wizline only reach gods of your level of invisibility and up (see 
<a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wiz</a>). It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Users</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wiz</a>
</pre>




</div>